Description: Fix overly broad D-Bus policy
 Remove the excessively permissive <allow send_type="method_call"/> rule
 from the default D-Bus policy context. The specific send_destination rules
 for org.synce.dccm are sufficient and avoid lintian error
 dbus-policy-excessively-broad.
Author: Gustavo Perez Reyes <ghreyes71@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-03-03

Index: synce-core-0.17/etc/org.synce.dccm.conf
===================================================================
--- synce-core-0.17.orig/etc/org.synce.dccm.conf
+++ synce-core-0.17/etc/org.synce.dccm.conf
@@ -13,7 +13,6 @@
 
   <!-- Allow anyone to invoke methods on the Device and DeviceManager interfaces -->
   <policy context="default">
-    <allow send_type="method_call"/>
     <allow send_destination="org.synce.dccm"
 	   send_interface="org.synce.dccm.Device"/>
 
